    "author_association": "NONE",
    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\n\n- [x] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\n- [x] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\n\n### Module(s)\n\nmini.pick\n\n### Description\n\nMy request is to be able to show filename_first for files and buffers. Sometimes paths can easily be covered by the size of the picker window (I know I can use <C-l> to move and see the rest) but it would be great to have a feature where the filename is shown first and then the directory part of the path.",
    "closed_at": "2025-12-20T16:11:57Z",
