        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "Thanks for the suggestion!\n\nI am afraid, I am not a big fan of showing filename separately at the beginning. The reasons are at least:\n- From usability point of view it probably requires alignment, but this is not ideal. Aligning based on all items will introduce a lot of unnecessary whitespace if there is a long file name out of view. While aligning based only on shown items will be a bit more flickery than I would have liked.\n- From implementation point of view it will inevitably require allowing to adjust how it must interact with icons (should be placed before or after?) and matching (should it take part in matching or not). Which is kind of a lot and 'mini.pick' is already very big.\n\nOne thing that I am open about is possibly introduce some sort of \"smart\" conceal of the long path. Not sure how to do that best yet. And since it is possible to scroll horizontally (which is indeed the suggested solution here), this is not a high priority.\n\nSo closing as not planned.\n\n---\n\nWith inline virtual text it can be implemented somewhat concisely like this:\n\n```lua\nlocal ns_id = vim.api.nvim_create_namespace('basename')\nlocal show_basename_first = function(buf_id, items_to_show, query)\n  vim.api.nvim_buf_clear_namespace(buf_id, ns_id, 0, -1)\n  MiniPick.default_show(buf_id, items_to_show, query, { show_icons = true })\n\n  local extmark_opts = { virt_text_pos = 'inline' }\n  for i = 1, #items_to_show do\n    extmark_opts.virt_text = { { vim.fs.basename(items_to_show[i]) .. ' ', 'Special' } }\n    vim.api.nvim_buf_set_extmark(buf_id, ns_id, i - 1, 0, extmark_opts)\n  end\nend\n\nlocal pick_opts = { source = { show = show_basename_first } }\nMiniPick.registry.files = function() MiniPick.builtin.files(nil, pick_opts) end\n```\n\nThe result looks like this:\n\n<img width=\"1802\" height=\"1049\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/54a10d99-87e9-4097-ba2c-d0a57912bec7\" />",
