        {
            "author_association": "NONE",
            "body": "Thanks for the quick reply, my idea was to have the icons first, then the filename and then the directory. I was playing around and come with this so far, although I am missing highlight of matched query.\n\nI don't know if there is a different way other than setting the buffer lines again.\n\n``` lua\nshow = function(buf_id, items_to_show, query)\n  vim.api.nvim_buf_clear_namespace(buf_id, ns_id, 0, -1)\n  pick.default_show(buf_id, items_to_show, query, { show_icons = true })\n  for i, item in ipairs(items_to_show) do\n    local tail = vim.fn.fnamemodify(item, ':t')\n    local head = vim.fn.fnamemodify(item, ':~:.:h')\n    if head == '.' then\n      head = ''\n    end\n    local icon, hl = MiniIcons.get('file', item)\n    local display = string.format('%s %s %s', icon, tail, head)\n    local line_nr = i - 1\n    vim.api.nvim_buf_set_lines(buf_id, line_nr, i, false, {display})\n    local icon_opts = { end_row = line_nr, end_col = 2, hl_mode = 'replace', hl_group = hl, priority = 199 }\n    vim.api.nvim_buf_set_extmark(buf_id, ns_id, line_nr, 0, icon_opts)\n    local head_opts = { end_row = i, end_col = 0, hl_mode = 'blend', hl_group = 'Comment', priority = 199 }\n    vim.api.nvim_buf_set_extmark(buf_id, ns_id, line_nr, #tail + 5, head_opts)\n  end\n```\nLooks like this:\n<img width=\"945\" height=\"541\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/f503523d-95ba-4392-927b-0e79528ebdd8\" />\n",
